      "side": 1,
      "message": "mConnector should be set with the mConnectorWaitQueue lock held in onTetheringConnected, otherwise it is possible that other threads call getConnector after this runs (but before the queue is drained) and receive a connector before the queue is drained. This would cause calls to be processed out-of-order.\n\nI think you can leave the code here as it was, just changing `connector !\u003d null` to `connector !\u003d null \u0026\u0026 connector.isBinderAlive()`, and un-commenting the assignment in onTetheringConnected.",
      "revId": "d7eb22803a3c44037bb86fef9bdf765f2bf7646d",
